# Shekel Budget App -- Docker build context: an ALLOWLIST
#
# Closes audit finding F-113 (ship only what the container runs) and plan
# step balance:X-do's BAL-625.  The Dockerfile's ``COPY --chown=shekel:shekel
# . .`` copies the WHOLE build context minus what this file excludes.  This
# file used to list what to leave out, so every new file shipped by default:
# by 2026-10-16 the image carried tools/, the linters' configs and host-only
# shell scripts beside the ones it named, and an image built from a host
# checkout also carried its lint cache and every ``__pycache__`` its runs had
# left (the bare ``__pycache__`` pattern matched only the context's root),
# while the file still named files since deleted.  Now ``*`` leaves
# out everything, and the ``!`` lines below bring back exactly what the image
# needs.  A file the image needs that is missing here fails loudly (the
# container cannot start, or the script is absent); a file wrongly shipped
# fails silently, which is why the default is out.
#
# Adding a file the container runs means adding its line here.  The
# docker-marked tests in tests/test_deploy/test_seed_credential_hygiene.py
# build the context with docker itself and grade what it holds.

*

# ── The application ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   app/              the Flask application package
#   run.py            the module gunicorn serves (Dockerfile CMD run:app)
#   gunicorn.conf.py  gunicorn's config (Dockerfile CMD)
#   entrypoint.sh     the image's ENTRYPOINT
#   migrations/       Alembic's history (scripts/init_database.py upgrades
#                     through app/migration_runner.py, which reads it and
#                     alembic.ini by path)
#   alembic.ini       Alembic's config
!app/
!run.py
!gunicorn.conf.py
!entrypoint.sh
!migrations/
!alembic.ini

# ── What entrypoint.sh runs at container start ─────────────────────
!scripts/init_db.sql
!scripts/init_db_role.sql
!scripts/init_database.py
!scripts/seed_user.py

# ── What an operator runs inside the container (the ``docker exec``
#    lines of docs/runbook.md, docs/runbook_secrets.md and
#    docs/backup_runbook.md; seed_companion.py by its own usage line),
#    and the modules those scripts import ────────────────────────────
!scripts/seed_ref_tables.py
!scripts/seed_companion.py
!scripts/audit_cleanup.py
!scripts/integrity_check.py
!scripts/_integrity_*.py
!scripts/reset_mfa.py
!scripts/rotate_sessions.py
!scripts/rotate_totp_key.py
!scripts/_script_lib.py

# ── Carried for the operator and the licence ───────────────────────
#   requirements.txt  stage 1's ``COPY requirements.txt .`` reads it from
#                     this same context (the build fails without it); the
#                     image keeps it for a ``pip freeze`` diff in an exec
#   .env.example      the configuration template docs/runbook_secrets.md
#                     rebuilds a .env from; never a real .env, which the
#                     last section leaves out wherever it sits
#   LICENSE           the BSD 3-Clause notice, which a redistribution in
#                     binary form must reproduce: the image is published
!requirements.txt
!.env.example
!LICENSE

# ── Never shipped, even from inside a directory brought back above ─
# The bytecode a host checkout's own runs leave beside the sources (Python
# compiles from the sources without it), a .env holding live credentials,
# and the suite's conftest.py.  Last, so they win over every ``!`` above;
# the template .env.example is brought back after its own exclusion.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[co]
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/conftest.py
